---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/ProgramLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/PageHero.astro';
import ProgramEnd from '../../../components/ProgramEnd.astro';
import Icon from '../../../components/Icon.astro';
import {space} from '../../../data/space';
---
<Layout track="space" section="overview" title="Space Technology & Satellite Systems" description="A multidisciplinary space technology learning track for students and college teams: mission design, subsystems, telemetry and educational demonstrators.">
<PageHero slot="hero" eyebrow="SPACE TECHNOLOGY / MULTIDISCIPLINARY LEARNING" title={space.headline} description={space.intro} image="space-tech" imageAlt="AI-generated learning scene with learners collaborating; not actual academy participants" caption="From a mission question to an educational demonstrator." />
<section class="container section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR DISCIPLINE HAS A PLACE</p><h2>A satellite is a team effort.</h2></div><p>Students bring different strengths. A shared mission gives those strengths a common interface, a practical problem and a reason to work together.</p></div><div class="opportunity-grid">{space.roles.map(([title,copy])=><article class="feature"><span class="feature-icon"><Icon name={title.startsWith('Mechanical')?'wrench':title.startsWith('Electronics')?'battery':title.startsWith('Computer')?'cpu':'brain'} /></span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="tinted section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">THE LEARNING JOURNEY</p><h2>Understand. Connect. Demonstrate.</h2><ol class="mission-flow">{space.modules.map((m,i)=><li><span>0{i+1}</span><h3>{m.title}</h3><p>{m.summary}</p></li>)}</ol><a class="text-link" href="/programs/space-technology/curriculum/">Explore modules, tools and practical work <Icon name="arrowRight" /></a></div></section>
<section class="container section two-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">FOR COLLEGES & STUDENT TEAMS</p><h2>Start with the team and the learning goal.</h2><p>A faculty coordinator can enquire for a mixed-discipline group. Discuss students’ current skills, learning objectives, available computers and any laboratory access, then agree a suitable teaching scope.</p><p>The baseline uses software simulation. A supervised bench-hardware extension can be discussed after trainer, equipment and facility availability are confirmed. Duration, fees and delivery arrangements remain enquiry-based.</p></div><article class="readiness-card"><h3>Bring to the first conversation</h3><ul class="check-list"><li>Disciplines, study years and approximate group size</li><li>Faculty coordinator and institution</li><li>Programming, electronics and design experience</li><li>Desired outcome: introduction, focused lab or integrated demonstrator</li><li>Available lab resources and access constraints</li></ul><p>Basic mathematics and curiosity about engineering systems are useful. Prior satellite-building experience is not assumed; bridge needs are discussed before teaching.</p></article></section>
<section class="container section section-tight"><div class="inline-note"><Icon name="compass" /><p><strong>Clear project scope.</strong> Planned learning opportunities focus on simulations and ground-based educational prototypes. Flight hardware qualification, satellite launch, radio operations and agency certification are outside the published program scope.</p></div></section><ProgramEnd track="space" />
</Layout>
<style>.opportunity-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:20px}.mission-flow{list-style:none;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:20px;padding:0;margin:32px 0}.mission-flow li{border-top:2px solid #637dc2;padding-top:18px}.mission-flow span{color:#4931ee;font-size:.8rem}.mission-flow h3{font-size:1.1rem;margin:12px 0}.mission-flow p{font-size:.85rem}@media(max-width:850px){.mission-flow{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:480px){.opportunity-grid,.mission-flow{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>